{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>See, I have made you Elohim.</b> That is: do not be concerned that you will not be heeded by Pharaoh, for I am making you great over him. And the import of the utterance, 'your brother Aaron shall be your prophet' — that is, he shall be the one who speaks. The expression 'your prophet' (נביאך) is in the sense of 'fruit of the lips' (ניב שפתים), and so Onkelos translated it as 'your interpreter' (מתורגמנך). And our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: 'See, I have made you Elohim to Pharaoh' — Pharaoh used to make himself out as a deity, as it is said (Ezekiel 29:3): 'The Nile is mine and I have made myself'; the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: since he makes himself out as a deity, let him be informed that he is nothing — behold, I am making you a deity over him."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:37.117716872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}